    {
      "id": "2095722578463592533",
      "text": "RT @niccruzpatane: The Tesla Cybercab doesn't have ANY brake fluid. It is the first production vehicle to have a brake-by-wire system. \n\nEl…",
      "created_at": "Fri Sep 04 03:56:14 +0000 2026",
      "lang": "en",
      "media": [],
      "retweet": {
        "id": "2095703149503762886",
        "text": "The Tesla Cybercab doesn't have ANY brake fluid. It is the first production vehicle to have a brake-by-wire system. \n\nElectronic actuators are responsible for the clamping pressure, rather than hydraulic fluid that you see in traditional vehicles.\n\nThis system improves efficiency since the brake pads can fully disengage. They can go entirely off or on. It also enables Tesla to fine-tune the braking to be as smooth as possible.\n\nPLUS, when the car is built with the unboxed process, Tesla doesn't need to run any brake lines, everything is seamless.",
        "created_at": "Fri Sep 04 02:39:01 +0000 2026",
        "lang": "en",
        "media": [
